        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lee Hong-gi, Dee Snider, Lee Soo-geun, Jeong Hyeong-don, Park Sung-kwang, Kim Jong-hyun, Chun Jung-myung\n- Organizations: Twisted Sister\n- Works: Night Goblin, Still Hungry, Strangeland, Horror-Teria, \"Heroes Are Hard to Find\"\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, actor, writer, fashion designer, screenwriter, radio personality\n\nFacts:\n- Dee Snider was born on March 15, 1955.\n- Dee Snider is an American singer-songwriter, screenwriter, radio personality, and actor.\n- In 1998, Twisted Sister recorded and released \"Heroes Are Hard to Find\" for the soundtrack of Strangeland.\n- Strangeland is a horror movie written by and starring Dee Snider.\n- Captain Howdy is a character from Horror-Teria on which Strangeland was based.\n- Lee Hong-gi is a South Korean singer-songwriter, actor, writer, and fashion designer.\n- Night Goblin is a South Korean television program starring Lee Soo-geun, Jeong Hyeong-don, Park Sung-kwang, Lee Hong-gi, Kim Jong-hyun, and Chun Jung-myung.",
